		{
			"id": "tvHFS4uRCffo09VxP",
			"name": "Unusual Background (Latent Psychic Potential)",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Psychic ability is a random, rare mutation of the human genome that lets its bearer perceive and touch the immaterium (the warp). Sources disagree on exact frequency — Imperial administrative texts and Dark Heresy-line background both describe it as \"rare but not vanishingly so,\" on the order of a handful of latent potentials per hive-sized population, with usably strong psykers far rarer still. Treat any precise ratio as flavour, not census data.\n\nDesign: Required to take Psyker (Talent), Warp Empowerment, or any trait carrying the Warp Sorcery power modifier below. Basic Set B261 leaves Unusual Background costs to the GM; 10 points reflects that the ability itself is not learned but grants access to an entire framework of further abilities, roughly the going rate other published settings use for \"you may buy from this power list at all.\"",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "tuCzv1SIsMOQY5anF",
			"name": "Warp Empowerment",
			"reference": "TSOR4",
			"local_notes": "A direct reskin of Sorcerous Empowerment (Thaumatology: Sorcery, TSOR4):\nthe psyker's raw, trained capacity to draw on and shape the warp, as\ndistinct from Psyker (Talent, TSOR5's Sorcery Talent analogue, below)\nwhich only sharpens related skills. Requires Unusual Background (Latent\nPsychic Potential). It is the prerequisite for every Warp Sorcery-tagged\nability in this file (see Witch-sight and each discipline below); the\nNavigator's Third Eye and the Pariah/Untouchable genes carry no Warp\nSorcery modifier and so need no Warp Empowerment.\n\nCap, cast per Thaumatology: Sorcery (TSOR): a psyker may only know a\npower whose full, modified point cost is no greater than the point cost\nof their own Warp Empowerment (10 + 10/level). A power bought at a\nhigher level (more dice, more range, etc.) costs proportionally more and\nmay outgrow a psyker's Empowerment even after they first learned it at a\ncheaper level — raising the level, and cost, of Warp Empowerment is how\na psyker \"grows into\" costlier or higher-level workings.\n\nImperial Assignment scale (Adeptus Astra Telepathica / Black Ships)\nmapped to Warp Empowerment level and the point cap that gives, worked\nout from this file's actual (Warp Sorcery -20% + Perils of the Warp)\nmodified costs:\n\n  Grade      | Empowerment level | Cap (10+10/lvl) | What the cap reaches\n  Iota       | 1                  | 20              | cheapest powers only: e.g. Smite (3), Endurance (2), Iron Arm (4), Fire Bolt (4), Assail (4), Mind Probe (14), Foresight (18) — register but rarely learn more than one or two\n  Zeta       | 1                  | 20              | as Iota; low Psyker Talent limits skill use, not what they can know\n  Eta        | 1                  | 20              | as Zeta\n  Theta      | 2                  | 30              | adds Molten Beam (9), Crush (11), Psychic Scream (12), Sanctuary (13), Null Zone (23), Terrify (28)\n  Epsilon    | 2                  | 30              | as Theta (typical Wyrdvane conscript)\n  Delta      | 3                  | 40              | adds Scrier's Gaze (35), Dominate (35), Gate of Infinity (40) — the full non-Great-Power roster (typical Sanctioned Primaris Psyker)\n  Gamma      | 3                  | 40              | as Delta, better skills from a higher Psyker Talent\n  Beta       | 4                  | 50              | full roster, with headroom to push a known leveled power to a higher level/more dice (many Astropaths)\n  Alpha      | 5                  | 60              | full roster, generous headroom for high-level workings (Astartes Librarians, Black Ship candidates)\n  Alpha-Plus | 7+ (GM only)       | 80+             | approaching Great Power territory; Vortex of Doom (280+ as usually bought) is still normally out of reach even here\n\nA character need not buy Warp Empowerment up to their grade's full\nceiling: templates in this project buy only the level their actually-\nknown powers need, and note the grade's theoretical ceiling separately.\n\nLore: The Iota-to-Alpha-Plus assignment scale is drawn from the Adeptus Astra Telepathica's own grading of psychic potential as depicted across Dark Heresy-line material and repeated in Codex/Imperial Armour background; Black Library uses the same grades in passing (e.g. Eisenhorn-cycle and Ciaphas Cain references to Alpha-class talents). \"Alpha-Plus\" specifically denotes the rarest, most dangerous talents the Black Ships process.\n\nDesign: Sorcerous Empowerment (TSOR4) costs 10 base + 10/level (level 1 = 20 points, each further level +10) in the GCS master Thaumatology data; reused verbatim here under a 40k-appropriate name, since the underlying mechanic — \"how much warp-power you can channel at all, gating which spells/powers you may know by their modified cost\" — is exactly what an Imperial Assignment grade represents. The level-to-grade mapping above is derived, not asserted: it walks every power in this file's actual modified cost (recomputed under the new Warp Sorcery -20% modifier, see below) and finds the cheapest Empowerment level whose cap clears it, so \"Iota can only cast minor powers\" and \"Alpha can cast the biggest non-Great-Power ability\" are literally true of the numbers, not just flavour text.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Talent",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"points_per_level": 10,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 1,
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "tc80_qeBGmgu8GAPA",
			"name": "Psyker",
			"reference": "TSOR5",
			"local_notes": "This project's Sorcery Talent (Thaumatology: Sorcery, TSOR5) analogue:\napplies as Sorcery Talent applies to a sorcerer's skills in TSOR, just\nto a 40k-specific list — Psyniscience, Meditation, Hidden Lore (the\nWarp), and the Will roll to resist Perils of the Warp (see above) — a\nhouse extension of Talent's normal \"add to listed skills\" rule,\nprecedented by Magery's and Sorcery Talent's own habit of aiding\nrelated rolls beyond pure spellcasting. Reaction bonus: +1/level from\nother sanctioned psykers and the Astra Telepathica.\n\nPsyker (Talent) and Warp Empowerment are separate purchases on separate\naxes, exactly as Sorcery Talent and Sorcerous Empowerment are in TSOR:\nthis trait only sharpens related skills and Perils resistance, while\nWarp Empowerment (above) is what actually gates which powers a psyker\nmay know. A high-Talent, low-Empowerment psyker is a sharp, well-drilled\nmind who simply hasn't learned much yet; the reverse is a raw prodigy\nwho is clumsy with the skills around their gift.\n\nImperial Assignment scale (Adeptus Astra Telepathica / Black Ships),\nweakest to strongest, mapped to Talent level. See Warp Empowerment above\nfor the matching Empowerment level/point-cap column, which is the real\ngate on ability selection:\n  Iota    — Talent 0 (latent; register but rarely take Psyker traits at all)\n  Zeta    — Talent 1\n  Eta     — Talent 1\n  Theta   — Talent 2\n  Epsilon — Talent 2  (typical Wyrdvane conscript)\n  Delta   — Talent 3  (typical Sanctioned Primaris Psyker)\n  Gamma   — Talent 4\n  Beta    — Talent 4  (many Astropaths)\n  Alpha   — Talent 5  (Astartes Librarians, Black Ship candidates)\n  Alpha-Plus — Talent 6+ (beyond-play tier: Primarchs,\n    the most powerful Inquisitors, the worst Chaos sorcerers)\n\nLore: The Iota-to-Alpha-Plus assignment scale is drawn from the Adeptus Astra Telepathica's own grading of psychic potential as depicted across Dark Heresy-line material and repeated in Codex/Imperial Armour background; Black Library uses the same grades in passing (e.g. Eisenhorn-cycle and Ciaphas Cain references to Alpha-class talents). \"Alpha-Plus\" specifically denotes the rarest, most dangerous talents the Black Ships process.\n\nDesign: Talent affecting four things (three skills plus the Perils resistance roll) sits at Basic's \"Medium Talent\" rate of 10 points/level (B90, three-to-five-skill bracket) rather than 5 (one-two skills) or 15 (six-nine skills) — the same rate Sorcery Talent itself uses (TSOR5, 10/level). Capped at level 6 for player characters; higher grades are GM-reference only, per the framework's \"Beyond play\" tier.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Talent",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"points_per_level": 10,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 2,
			"base_points": 0,
			"max_levels": 6
		},
		{
			"id": "t2MpNDJiY68hh3D84",
			"name": "Warp Blast",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Zoanthrope's signature attack: a crackling bolt of raw psychic force hurled from its forehead that burns through armour as readily as flesh — the bioform's entire battlefield purpose across every Codex edition and the reason a Zoanthrope brood is treated as priority artillery in Black Library's Hive Fleet fiction.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Burning, 5/die, B61) with Armor Divisor (2) (+50%, B103, matching this project's Necron gauss-tier armour-piercing convention) plus the standard Warp Sorcery/Perils pair, net +20%. Full modified cost: 5 x 1.2 = 6 points/level; needs Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20).",
